## 6. Linear Search

Linear search checks each item one by one.

### Simple Definition

```text
Linear search checks each element in sequence until the target is found or the list ends.
```

### Works On

```text
unsorted data
sorted data
arrays
ArrayLists
linked lists
```

### Pseudocode

```text
found ← false
index ← 0

WHILE index < length(items) AND found = false
    IF items[index] = target THEN
        found ← true
    ELSE
        index ← index + 1
    ENDIF
ENDWHILE

OUTPUT found
```

### Mark Scheme Phrase

```text
Linear search can be used on unsorted data because it checks each item one at a time.
```

---

