## 10. Binary Search

Binary search works on sorted data.

### Simple Definition

```text
Binary search repeatedly compares the target with the middle item of a sorted list and discards half of the remaining search space.
```

### Requirements

```text
data must be sorted
random/index access is usually needed
```

### Pseudocode

```text
low ← 0
high ← length(items) - 1
found ← false

WHILE low <= high AND found = false
    mid ← (low + high) DIV 2

    IF items[mid] = target THEN
        found ← true
    ELSE IF target < items[mid] THEN
        high ← mid - 1
    ELSE
        low ← mid + 1
    ENDIF
ENDWHILE

OUTPUT found
```

### Mark Scheme Phrase

```text
Binary search is more efficient for large sorted lists because it halves the search space after each comparison.
```

---

