## 13. Why Binary Search Needs Sorted Data

Binary search decides which half of the list to discard by comparing the target with the middle value.

If the data is not sorted, this decision is invalid.

### Example

```text
[10, 3, 21, 7, 15]
```

If middle is `21` and target is `15`, binary search might discard the wrong half because the order is not meaningful.

### Exam Phrase

```text
Binary search requires sorted data because it uses the ordering to decide whether the target must be in the lower or upper half.
```

