## 16. Bubble Sort

Bubble sort repeatedly compares adjacent items and swaps them if they are in the wrong order.

### Simple Definition

```text
Bubble sort compares adjacent values and swaps them if they are out of order, repeating passes until the list is sorted.
```

### Pseudocode

```text
FOR pass ← 0 TO length(items) - 2
    FOR index ← 0 TO length(items) - 2 - pass
        IF items[index] > items[index + 1] THEN
            temp ← items[index]
            items[index] ← items[index + 1]
            items[index + 1] ← temp
        ENDIF
    ENDFOR
ENDFOR
```

### Key Idea

After each pass, the largest remaining item moves to its correct position at the end.

---

