## 20. Selection Sort

Selection sort repeatedly selects the smallest remaining item and places it in the next correct position.

### Simple Definition

```text
Selection sort finds the smallest unsorted item and swaps it into the next position.
```

### Pseudocode

```text
FOR start ← 0 TO length(items) - 2
    minIndex ← start

    FOR index ← start + 1 TO length(items) - 1
        IF items[index] < items[minIndex] THEN
            minIndex ← index
        ENDIF
    ENDFOR

    temp ← items[start]
    items[start] ← items[minIndex]
    items[minIndex] ← temp
ENDFOR
```

### Key Idea

The sorted section grows from the left.

---

## 21. Trace Selection Sort

### Data

```text
[5, 2, 4, 1]
```

### Pass 1

Smallest from indexes 0-3 is `1`.

Swap with index 0:

```text
[1, 2, 4, 5]
```

### Pass 2

Smallest from indexes 1-3 is `2`.

Already in position:

```text
[1, 2, 4, 5]
```

### Pass 3

Smallest from indexes 2-3 is `4`.

Already in position:

```text
[1, 2, 4, 5]
```

### Final

```text
[1, 2, 4, 5]
```

