## 22. Insertion Sort

Insertion sort builds a sorted section one item at a time.

### Simple Definition

```text
Insertion sort takes each item and inserts it into the correct position within the already sorted part of the list.
```

### Pseudocode

```text
FOR index ← 1 TO length(items) - 1
    current ← items[index]
    position ← index - 1

    WHILE position >= 0 AND items[position] > current
        items[position + 1] ← items[position]
        position ← position - 1
    ENDWHILE

    items[position + 1] ← current
ENDFOR
```

### Key Idea

The left part of the list is kept sorted.

---

## 23. Trace Insertion Sort

### Data

```text
[5, 2, 4, 1]
```

### Insert 2

```text
[2, 5, 4, 1]
```

### Insert 4

Move 5 right, insert 4:

```text
[2, 4, 5, 1]
```

### Insert 1

Move 5, 4, 2 right, insert 1:

```text
[1, 2, 4, 5]
```

### Final

```text
[1, 2, 4, 5]
```

