## 24. Sorting Algorithm Comparison

| Feature | Bubble Sort | Selection Sort | Insertion Sort |
|---|---|---|---|
| Main idea | swap adjacent items | select smallest remaining | insert into sorted part |
| Simple to trace | yes | yes | medium |
| Good for nearly sorted data | optimized version can be good | not especially | often good |
| Number of swaps | can be many | usually fewer | shifts elements |
| Common exam focus | adjacent comparisons and swaps | min index and swap | shifting and insertion |

### Exam Phrase

```text
Bubble sort repeatedly swaps adjacent out-of-order values, selection sort repeatedly selects the smallest remaining value, and insertion sort inserts each value into its correct position in a sorted section.
```

