## 25. Choosing a Search or Sort

| Scenario | Suitable Choice | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| unsorted small list | linear search | simple and no sorting needed |
| large sorted list | binary search | halves search space |
| list changes often and is unsorted | linear search | sorting repeatedly may not be worth it |
| user wants names alphabetically | sorting | improves readability |
| leaderboard high to low | sorting descending | ranks players |
| nearly sorted list | insertion sort | often efficient on nearly sorted data |
| simple classroom trace | bubble sort | easy to see swaps |
| few swaps desired | selection sort | swaps once per pass |

