## 26. Common Search Errors

| Error | Why It Happens | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| binary search on unsorted data | halves may not contain target | sort data first or use linear search |
| loop never updates index | infinite loop | increment/decrement properly |
| binary search mid not recalculated | wrong range checked | recalculate mid each loop |
| using `<` instead of `<=` | may miss last remaining item | use `low <= high` |
| not stopping after found | extra work or wrong updates | use found flag / return |
| high/low update reversed | discards wrong half | compare target with middle carefully |
| not handling empty list | index errors | check length first |
| string comparison mistake in Java | `==` checks reference | use `.equals()` |
| starting index wrong | misses first element | start at 0 for zero-based lists |
| final not-found not output | incomplete answer | output false/not found after loop |

---

## 27. Common Sorting Errors

| Error | Why It Happens | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| comparing wrong pair | index confusion | compare adjacent items for bubble sort |
| loop goes one step too far | index + 1 out of range | stop at length - 2 |
| swap missing temporary variable | one value overwritten | use temp |
| selection sort minIndex not reset | wrong minimum chosen | set minIndex = start each pass |
| insertion sort loses current value | overwritten during shifting | store current first |
| sorting ascending vs descending confused | comparison sign wrong | use `>` for ascending bubble swap |
| output after each comparison when not asked | noisy output | output final list unless trace asked |
| sorting strings as numbers | wrong comparison | compare according to data type |
| assumes one pass fully sorts | usually false | repeat passes |
| ignores already sorted optimization | less efficient | use swapped flag if required |

