## 28. Worked Example: Binary Search Pseudocode Explanation

### Question

Explain this section:

```text
IF target < items[mid] THEN
    high ← mid - 1
ELSE
    low ← mid + 1
ENDIF
```

### Answer

If the target is smaller than the middle value, it cannot be in the upper half of a sorted ascending list, so the high boundary moves to the item before the middle. If the target is larger, the low boundary moves to the item after the middle. This halves the remaining search space.

---

## 29. Worked Example: Swap

### Problem

Swap `items[index]` and `items[index + 1]`.

### Correct Swap

```text
temp ← items[index]
items[index] ← items[index + 1]
items[index + 1] ← temp
```

### Why Temp Is Needed

Without `temp`, one of the values may be overwritten before it is copied.

